\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Relationship-token verification from the frozen implementation. The baseline branch needs original process, authentication, and network claims with three distinct roots. Only a \texttt  {missing\_family} rejection can enter the fallback branch, which needs original authentication and network claims, plus an original endpoint root distinct from both. The paths share identity, temporal, causal-field, component-context, and size constraints. Failure retains the existing partition; the diagram omits evaluator truth because it is unavailable to prediction.}}{4}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:verify}{{6}{4}{Relationship-token verification from the frozen implementation. The baseline branch needs original process, authentication, and network claims with three distinct roots. Only a \texttt {missing\_family} rejection can enter the fallback branch, which needs original authentication and network claims, plus an original endpoint root distinct from both. The paths share identity, temporal, causal-field, component-context, and size constraints. Failure retains the existing partition; the diagram omits evaluator truth because it is unavailable to prediction}{figure.caption.8}{}}
